// Air Bombardment & Secondary Barrage Targets Table (§41.5, PDF p107 + key p108). Total weapon
// points (Bomb Points, or Torpedo Points only vs the Commonwealth Fleet — key note a) pick a
// column; a 2d6 roll (encoded 10*d1+d2, monotonic with the 11..66 dice order) read on the target
// group's rows gives the result. Rows are ordered by increasing result; `ranges[col]` is None (no
// such result in that column) or Some((min,max)) 2d6.
//
// Result meanings (key, p108): Airfield = SGSUs that may no longer use the field's readying
// capacity (capacity levels reduced); Air Landing Strip = eliminated on any result >=1; Port =
// efficiency levels lost; Supply Dump = percent of all supplies eliminated (+1 Truck Point per
// 10%); Trucks = truck points (+cargo) destroyed; Flak Suppression = AA TOE points eliminated;
// Combat Units = battalion-(then company-)equivalents pinned (§41.9); Commonwealth Fleet = damage
// points; Axis Naval Convoy = percent of shipping eliminated; Fortification = reduced one level or
// not; Railroad = destroyed or not; Road = reduced to a track or not. Modifier: subtract one from
// a Land Support Bombing result against armor units (applied in code).
(
    bomb_bands:    [20, 40, 80, 120, 160, 200, 260, 320, 390, 470, 4294967295],
    torpedo_bands: [5, 12, 24, 50, 80, 120, 160, 210, 270, 340, 4294967295],
    // §12.53 Artillery Barrage Points column (§41.5 header row b, PDF p107). 21+ maxes at the
    // 391-470 (index 9) column; the 471+ column is unreachable by barrage.
    barrage_bands: [2, 4, 6, 10, 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 4294967295],

    // Airfields / Air Landing Strips / Ports (result = level count 0..4).
    airfield_port_strip: [
        (result: 0, ranges: [Some((11,62)),Some((11,55)),Some((11,51)),Some((11,42)),Some((11,36)),Some((11,31)),Some((11,15)),Some((11,12)),None,None,None]),
